# LinkedIn message: {{COMPANY}} — {{ROLE}}

> Read `profile/style_guide.md` and the original `profile/voice_samples/`.
> Default to a connection note and follow-up DM only when both are actually useful.

## Formats

- Connection note: up to 300 characters.
- DM: usually a short natural paragraph or two; below 200 words.
- InMail: only if requested or useful; still keep it concise.
- If the user is already connected, write a DM rather than pretending this is a new connection request.

Write to the actual person and the actual context. State the relevant role or work, why this recipient is being contacted, and any appropriate next step. Use only supported facts.

Do not force a 'who I am / mutually valuable connection / call to action' structure. Do not invent a prior relationship, say you have been following someone's work without evidence, or present an unsolicited three-bullet pitch. Avoid generic opening pleasantries and stock LinkedIn phrasing.

If the user requests one message type, output only that type.
